Digital and Information Builders Announce FOCUS Computing Tools - Press Release

 DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION AND INFORMATION BUILDERS ANNOUNCE
          UNIX BASED ENTERPRISE CLIENT/SERVER COMPUTING TOOLS

     Firms to Cooperate in Developing FOCUS for Open Environments
           and FOCUS Reporter for Motif for Alpha platforms

 MAYNARD, Mass. -- January 13, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation and
 Information Builders have signed an agreement to develop advanced
 releases of FOCUS for Digital's Alpha systems running the DEC OSF/1
 operating system, Digital's UNIX. FOCUS is a leading set of tools for
 developing enterprise-wide reporting applications which scale from
 workgroups to high-end servers.

 Digital will be providing Information Builders with resources for
 software and sales development, and will contribute its technical
 expertise and support to Information Builders' software engineering
 development process.

 "UNIX is the preferred operating environment for many organizations
 moving from mainframe to client/server environments," said John
 O'Keefe, vice president of UNIX systems marketing for Digital.  "The
 FOCUS tools will let customers benefit from one of the most
 comprehensive and portable development and reporting capabilities in
 the industry and empower users to employ data more strategically."

 Two components to be released

 The companies will work jointly on two FOCUS elements: FOCUS for Open
 Environments and FOCUS Reporter for Motif. FOCUS for Open Environments
 provides users with parallel query capability to fully exploit SMP
 systems, allowing FOCUS to scale from small workgroups to powerful
 high-end servers. FOCUS Reporter for Motif will enable Digital's UNIX
 customers to utilize client/server technology to develop sophisticated,
 GUI-based reports.

 "Digital's Alpha systems are the clear price/performance leaders
 today," said Mike Flom, general manager, Digital Division, Information
 Builders. "And DEC OSF/1 has been identified as the most standard,
 high-quality UNIX available. We are pleased to work together with
 Digital to provide a high level of enterprise-wide, client/server
 functionality to UNIX customers.  That functionality gives users what
 they need to resolve some of the critical business issues they face
 when rightsizing and reengineering their corporate computing
 environments."

 FOCUS for Open Environments Exploits Parallel Query Technology

 The latest release of FOCUS for DEC OSF/1 is FOCUS for Open
 Environments. This advanced release includes a broad set of
 enhancements in the areas of SMP-exploitive technology, RDBMS
 interfaces, data migration tools and integrated Postscript support. Of
 these enhancements, the most significant is parallel query technology,
 which allows client/server applications to exploit the processing power
 of SMP systems, including many of the AlphaServer systems.

 Parallel query technology enables FOCUS DBMS users to increase
 throughput, exploiting all processors on today's SMP systems by
 dividing users' queries into sections that can be processed in parallel
 on multiple processors, and running in parallel on FOCUS' native
 database.

 FOCUS Reporter for Motif

 FOCUS Reporter for Motif is a graphical client/server reporting and
 decision support application development toolset that allows developers
 and end-users to develop, integrate and transparently move applications
 between Motif, Windows and character-based environments. FOCUS Reporter
 for Motif provides full portability and interoperability with FOCUS
 Reporter for Windows, Information Builders PC-based graphical reporting
 and decision support tool. It is also fully compatible with character-
 based versions of FOCUS on all platforms.

 Other features include:

    New interfaces for the latest versions of Sybase, Oracle, and
    Informix

    RDBMS Auto Facilities with increased functionality, intelligence for
    defining relational data

    Data migration tools that allow for the seamless rightsizing of data
    stored in FOCUS.

    Integrated PostScript support

 FOCUS for Open Environments will be available in the third quarter of
 1995. FOCUS Reporter for Motif on DEC OSF/1 will be available by the
 end of the year. Pricing is user based and will range from $1,895 for a
 single user to approximately $140,000 for 128 users utilizing eight
 processors. Enterprise licensing is also available.

 Information Builders, a privately held company, was incorporated in
 1975 and ranks among the top independent software vendors in the world,
 with 1993 revenues of $227 million. The firm's integrated products and
 services provide open solutions to enterprise needs for business
 intelligence and data access. These solutions, available worldwide,
 incorporate FOCUS (the world's leading 4GL), EDA/SQL (industry's top
 middleware), and Level5 expert system technologies.

 Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open
 client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide
 information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, storage,
 networking, software and services, together with industry-focused
 solutions from business partners, help organizations compete and win in
 today's global marketplace.

