ICS Builder Xcessory on DEC OSF/1, SunOS, Solaris 2, HP/700, and SGI

HIGHLIGHTS

o This graphical user interface building tool replaces Digital's VUIT
  product, which has been discontinued

o V3.5 integrates with more development tools and environments than any
  other graphical user interface building tool

o The product enables developers to build graphical user interfaces quickly
  and easily while working in a familiar environment

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

ICS Builder Xcessory V3.5 is a graphical user interface building tool for
Motif. It is a replacement for Digital's VUIT product, which was
discontinued in 1993.

Builder Xcessory integrates with more tools and more environments than any
other graphical user interface building tool. V3.5 now integrates into the
DEC FUSE, SunSoft WorkShop, and SGI CASEVision environments. In addition,
Builder Xcessory integrates with some of the best development tools
available, including CodeCenter, ObjectCenter, Purify, XRunner, RCS, and
SCCS. This gives developers the ability to continue working in the
environment they are accustomed to, while expanding it to meet the needs
associated with building graphical user interfaces quickly and easily.

Object oriented design is all about building re-usable parts and re-using
them. Builder Xcessory enables developers to create their own re-usable
Motif environment. Classes, collections, styles, and constants can all be
saved in Builder Xcessory and are then accessible to developers for future
use. These features are available to all developers using Builder Xcessory
-- not just those doing C++ development. No matter what language is
generated from Builder Xcessory (C, C++, or UIL), users reap the benefits of
the object oriented design environment and the modularity of code that
Builder Xcessory generates.

The latest version of Builder Xcessory also increases ease of use by adding
Multiple Select, the ability to view and modify compound widget children,
quick access menus, and a search in the Browser tree. Whether users are
novices or experts with Motif, Builder Xcessory can help them build better
applications faster.

Not only can users create wonderful Motif based applications, but developers
can also add Work Procedures (functions that get called when the interface
of a Motif application is idle) and Timers (functions that get called after
a specific amount of time has elapsed) to their applications through Builder
Xcessory. Developers can also add widgets (bought or developed) to the
Palette of Builder Xcessory to further expand their repetoire of user
interface building blocks.

BENEFITS

o  Fits into any development environment

o  Offers a full object oriented design environment

o  Easy to use

o  Goes beyond Motif

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Builder Xcessory V3.5 is available now on DEC OSF/1 platforms (DEC OSF/1
V2.0 and later) and will be available on OpenVMS VAX and AXP platforms
(OpenVMS AXP V1.5, V6.1, and later; OpenVMS VAX V5.5-2, V6.0, and later) in
the Spring of 1995.

