Because the kernels of DYNA3D code span multiple subroutines,
cross compilation optimization is suggested. There are three ways
to do this: inlining, interprocedural analysis, and directives
specifying that the inner subroutines can be concurrentized.
Using KAP's inlining capability gives KAP the most freedom to
optimize the program because in this manner KAP can restructure
code across subroutines.

Figure 4 shows part of the call sequence of subroutine SOLDE.
(Subroutine SOLDE contains call sequence (b) of Table 4.)
Subroutine SOLDE calls subroutine HRGMD which calls subroutine
