DECserver 900GM 32-Port Network Access Server

HIGHLIGHTS

o  "Flash ready" 32-port DECserver product for DEChub 900 multiswitch

o  Supports both full and partial modem control in a single chassis

o  Bulk connectors for cable management and Telco wiring environments

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The DECserver 900GM multi-protocol server supports DECserver Network Access
Software V1.5 (SPD 46.13), providing support for protocols including LAT,
TCP/IP, Telnet, SLIP, CSLIP, point-to-point protocol (PPP), TN3270, Kerberos
security, and the enhanced DECserver user interface.

The DECserver 900GM is configured with four 68-pin connectors, each of which
can be configured individually via software to support one of several modes
of signaling. For users who require full RS232 modem control, each port can
be configured to support four users. For users who need partial modem
control, each port can be configured to support one of two sets of modem
control signals supporting eight users per port. In addition, sixty-eight
50-pin adapters are included with the DECserver 900GM, allowing direct
connection into 50-pin Telco wiring environments.

The DECserver 900GM is a high performance hardware platform configured with
4 MB of memory and expandable to 8 MB with user installable SIMM memory
cards. The DECserver 900GM is "flash ready," meaning it has an externally
accessible socket for a user installable flash card option. The flash card
provides the server with the capability to boot itself without needing a
load host.

The DECserver 900GM provides high port speed and throughput, expandable
memory, and upgradable flash capability. It also supports the continuously
expanding array of new applications provided through software enhancements
to DECserver Network Access Software.

BENEFITS

o  Supports DECserver Network Access Software V1.5 -- Proven, evolving,
   multi-protocol, multi-application software.

o  Flexible, asynchronous interface design -- Supports multiple signaling
   models from full to partial modem control.

o  Supports Digital NetRider client software packages -- Provides a complete
   client/server solution for remote PC access to IP, IPX, and AppleTalk
   networks, or to the Internet.

o  Telco 50-pin adapters included -- Direct connection to building wiring
   environments.

o  High performance -- Line speeds up to 115.2 Kbits per second per port;
   can support PC dial-up applications.

o  External flash card option -- No need for a load host to down-line load
   the software.

o  Expandable memory to 8 MB -- Able to support software enhancements.

o  Full modem control signaling RTS, CTS, DSR, DCD, SMI, DTR, RI, and DSRS
   -- Able to support all modem applications on any port.

o  Software selectable limited modem control signaling (medium high speed:
   DTR, DSR, RTS, and CTS; low medium speed: DTR, DSRS, DCD, and RI) -- Able
   to support most users per port.

o  DEChub 900 Multiswitch "max module" packaging -- Same server supports
   standalone or DEChub 900 installation for configuration flexibility.

