DECNIS 500 and 600 Routers Plus Management Processor and High-speed Cards

HIGHLIGHTS

o  DECNIS Management Processor Card (MPC-II) has a console port and more
   memory

o  High-speed synchronous DEC WANcontroller 622/HS card supports 2 lines,
   each at up to 10 Mb per second

o  DECNIS 500-SPX and 600-SPX base router platforms are available with the
   new DECNIS Management Processor Card

o  New pricing for DECNIS services

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The new DECNIS Management Processor Card, referred to as the MPC-II,
provides a console port with a 25-pin D type connector and full modem
control for out-of-band management. It also has 16 MB of dynamic memory and
4 MB of Flash memory. This allows greater flexibility when configuring
network parameters, and allows multiple configuration files to be stored in
Flash memory.

The new DECNIS MPC-II card is orderable as an add-on and is also included in
two new base router platforms -- the four-slot DECNIS 500-SPX and the
six-slot DECNIS 600-SPX. These platforms also include DECNIS chassis and a
pool memory card.

The new DEC WANcontroller 622/HS high-speed synchronous card provides two
interfaces, each running at line speeds of up to 12 Mb per second, and
supports connections to V.35, RS422, and X.21 interfaces via adapter cables.
The card supports both routing and bridging over leased lines (PPP or HDLC)
and Frame Relay; and routing over SMDS DXI at up to a 16 Mb per second class
of service. It can also be used with inverse multiplexor equipment to
combine a number of T1 links into a single higher-speed link.

BENEFITS

o  The MPC-II card allows out-of-band management of DECNIS routers using the
   console port, via either a direct terminal connection or a dial-up modem
   connection.

o  The console supports secure access via password authentication, access to
   the NCL (Network Command Language) command line interface, and the
   ability to manage multiple configuration files in the MPC-II Flash
   memory.

o  The DEC WANcontroller 622/HS card supports two lines, each running at up
   to 12 Mb per second -- allowing an up to 24 Mb per second full duplex
   data transfer to be supported. SMDS DXI is supported at up to a 16 Mb per
   second class of service.

o  The DEC WANcontroller 622/HS card can be used with inverse multiplexor
   equipment for connecting to multiple T1 lines. This improves network
   resilience because if a T1 link is lost, the remaining T1 links are still
   available.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The new DECNIS MPC-II card, platforms, and the DEC WANcontroller 622/HS card
and packages are available now through Digital and its business partners.

The DECNIS MPC-II card is orderable as an add-on and is also included in the
DECNIS 500-SPX and 600-SPX router platforms. Users who wish to upgrade their
existing DECNIS units can exchange their old MPC-I cards for the new MPC-II
card at a reduced price.

The DECNIS 500-SPX and 600-SPX include DECNIS chassis, the new MPC-II card
with console port, and a pool memory card. Network interface cards can be
ordered separately.

The DEC WANcontroller 622/HS is available with or without adapter cables;
V.35, RS422, and X.21 packages include the appropriate adapter cables.

