DECNIS V3.0 Software for DECNIS 500 and 600 Router Platforms

HIGHLIGHTS

o  A "virtual router cluster" capability and "resilient routing circuits"
   feature greatly improve resilience in backbone routing environments

o  V3.0 software is designed for use with the new MPC-II card, which
   provides out-of-band management capability; and the new DEC WANcontroller
   622/HS card, which supports new high-speed services

o  Packet prioritization and pattern matching capabilities provide better
   utilization of WAN links

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

DECNIS V3.0 software provides a number of new features for the high
performance DECNIS 500-SPX and 600-SPX (see separate article in this issue)
multiprotocol backbone routers. These new features greatly improve network
resilience and redundancy in mission critical network environments.

DECNIS V3.0 is designed for use with the new MPC-II and DEC WANcontroller
622/HS cards (see article DECNIS 500 and 600 Routers Plus Management
Processor and High-speed Cards). The MPC-II card provides out-of-band
management capability. The DEC WANcontroller 622/HS card provides support
for new high-speed WAN services such as Switched Multi-megabit Data Service
(SMDS).

BENEFITS

o  The virtual router cluster function allows a group of DECNIS routers to
   be defined as a routing cluster in which members of the cluster act as
   fast backup or standby routers to each other, should a router become
   unavailable.

o  The resilient routing circuits feature allows secondary circuits to be
   established automatically only for the duration of a primary circuit
   failure.

o  A packet prioritization capability allows different traffic types to be
   prioritized over low bandwidth WAN links; and provides simple packet
   filtering.

o  A pattern matching function allows packets containing specific bit fields
   to be filtered, thereby reducing network costs.

o  Using the new DEC WANcontroller 622/HS card, SMDS DXI allows routing at
   speeds up to a 16 Mb per second class of service.

o  Out-of-band management capability and ability to store multiple
   configuration files are provided using the new MPC-II card.

o  IPXWAN routing provides native Novell IPX over PPP datalinks for
   interoperability with other vendors' routers.

