VELOCITOR Controller Available on PCI Bus for UNIX Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Two-channel controller doubles performance per connection

o  Supports PCI bus with a high capacity of 47.5 GB per connection

o  Supports the AlphaServer 2100 processor with DEC OSF/1 platform

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The newest Alpha systems are based on the PCI bus. PCI is a new bus
architecture, and relatively few high performance storage options are
currently available. Current SCSI technology has not matched the processing
power of the Alpha family of computers. Although Digital has high
performance disk storage options on TURBOchannel and Futurebus+ devices,
there has been no upgrade path from the current IPI (Intelligent Peripheral
Interface) storage technology on Digital's Alpha processors.

The power of the new Alpha systems can be enhanced by the performance of the
VELOCITOR I/O subsystem. The new VELOCITOR solution from Digital combines
very fast storage controllers and disks to handle the demands of the Alpha
systems and I/O intensive applications. With controller-based disk striping,
the effects of multiple disks and two channels can be combined to yield a
higher sustained data rate. This is especially significant in matching the
speeds that can be obtained with the new Alpha systems. It is the ideal
solution for large streams of data where block mode can be employed. Any
application doing image processing or requiring large amounts of data will
benefit from this solution.

The new VELOCITOR controller is a two-channel controller. Performance
benchmarks have shown the controller can deliver a sustainable data rate of
24 MB per second. It also supports up to 8 disk drives per channel for a
high capacity of 47.5 GB per port. Included in the package are
controller-based striping and shadowing capabilities. The controller has
been developed to reduce I/O wait states through intelligent caching, seek
and latency ordering, and read ahead buffering. The VELOCITOR PCI-based
controller currently supports the AlphaServer 2100 4/200 processor. Other
PCI-based processor support will be added over time.

Digital provides a migration path to PCI for the TURBOchannel and Futurebus+
VELOCITOR users. The new industry-standard PCI bus will have many more
devices connected to it than will proprietary solutions. VELOCITOR
performance can use all the PCI bandwidth of this bus and still have I/O
performance in reserve to match future performance of the bus. When the size
of the record is large and the amount of transfer data is large, VELOCITOR
performance may be the key to performance success. As more and more data
becomes translated into calculated images, scanned images, video files, and
audio files, VELOCITOR products will offer the throughput needed for these
large sequential files.

BENEFITS

o  Provides unmatched I/O performance to handle near realtime applications

o  Provides disk investment protection for users using TURBOchannel or
   Futurebus+ machines today with an intent to migrate to new PCI-based
   AlphaGeneration technology in the future

o  Provides fast data throughput to prevent I/O waits or bottlenecks

VELOCITOR Controller on the PCI Bus

