Simplified Ordering of StorageWorks RAID Array 210 Subsystem for Alpha

The StorageWorks RAID Array 210 subsystem is a hardware-based RAID subsystem
for Alpha and Intel system platforms that use the industry standard EISA
bus. It provides RAID levels 0 (striping), 1 (mirroring), 0+1 (striped
mirrored sets), and 5 (striping with distributed parity). By providing RAID
functionality, it binds a collection of disk drives into a smaller number of
logical drives to provide data redundancy and increased performance.

For more information on the StorageWorks RAID Array 210 subsystem, please
see the "StorageWorks RAID Array 210" article in the April 11, 1994 issue of
Customer Update and the current Systems and Options Catalog.

The StorageWorks RAID Array 210 subsystem was introduced in March 1994. When
it was introduced, users selected either an SWXCR-EA or SWXCR-EB RAID
controller, plus one of three Software Documentation Kits (for OpenVMS AXP,
DEC OSF/1, or Windows NT platforms). This resulted in a total of five part
numbers. Effective immediately, there will now be one part number combining
the software and the RAID controller. Now users will only have to specify
whether they need the single or three SCSI channel RAID controller. The
software for all three Alpha operating systems will be included with the
controller.

The StorageWorks RAID Array 210 Subsystem for Alpha systems is available
now.

