PowerWare Prestige 3000 and 6000 Series Online Modular UPS Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Only online UPS with hot swap, plug and play, lightweight, modular
   design; Series 6000 models are upgradeable from 4.5 to 6 kVA

o  Premium performance including widest input voltage range and longest
   battery life

o  OnliNet monitoring and shutdown software for safe CPU shutdown and full
   network power management and control in SNMP or NMS environments

o  Exclusive, three-year hot-swap return warranty with a 24-hour turnaround;
   five-year onsite pick-up and exchange upgrade available

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The PowerWare Prestige Series 3000, which is available in 3 kVA, and 6000,
which is available in 4.5 and 6 kVA, are a revolutionary breakthrough in
online uninterruptable power protection. Unlike traditional online designs,
the unit is made up of three lightweight, plug and play modules that can be
easily diagnosed and swapped out or upgraded by the user:

o  The Electronics Module containing the inverter, automatic bypass, and
   communications intelligence.
o  The Battery Module, which can be monitored visually or through the
   software.
o  The Powerpass Distribution Module, which provides a maintenance bypass
   function and allows the electronics to be safely disconnected without
   interrupting the critical load.

The standard international version does not currently include the Powerpass
Distributuion Module.

The Prestige North American unit is available in both 208 or 240 volts input
and 120, 120/208, 120/240 VAC (Volt Alternating Current) output models. The
international unit is switch selectable for 208, 220, 230, and 240 input and
output voltage.

These systems are intended to protect critical computing and networking
applications that require continuous access during any power anomaly. The
products satisfy power protection needs for servers, telecommunications,
networking, and workstation environments.

Digital is selling the Prestige Series 3000 and 6000 under the logo of a
business partner, Exide Electronics, who will provide warranty service.

Features

Double-conversation, microprocessor controlled technology provides
regenerated, clean power at all times for consistent performance during the
worst voltage fluctuations, brownouts, or blackouts. This performance is
backed by Exide's $25,000 Powerware Protection Guarantee (see the Service
section for more information).

The user-friendly front panel features visual and audible alarms for battery
failure, overload, and change of state. Status indicators include LED bar
graph display of percent load, battery time remaining, and operational
status. The unit also provides an automatic battery self-test feature.

An exclusive online design extends battery life, and the "Cell Saver"
utility interface gives the Series 3000 and 6000 the ability to accept lower
input voltages when the UPS load is at less than 100 percent capacity. The
battery is used only during the most severe brownouts and blackouts,
enabling the unit to run cooler and substantially increasing battery life.

The modular battery packs of the Prestige models can be changed, added, or
removed without turning off the UPS -- providing regulated online power
while the battery is being serviced or upgraded.

The Powerpass Distribution Module houses an isolation transformer to provide
full galvanic isolation while on auto or maintenance bypass. This feature
eliminates unwanted harmonics in the building distribution system and,
unlike competitive products, there is no need to have the input voltage
match the output voltage in bypass.

The Powerpass Distribution Module also contains the output receptacles and
protects the critical load by allowing it to be manually transferred to the
utilty power source (bypass) without interruption. Extra output receptacles
are provided by extendable plug-in distribution modules. Each receptacle has
individual circuit breaker protection for maximum flexibility. The modules
are UL 1778 approved for safe handling.

The Prestige units are manufactured in accordance with ISO9001 standards for
quality throughout the design, documentation, and manufacturing processes.
All models meet UL, CSA, and IEC safety specifications, and are FCC and CDC
compliant for EMC verification.

Positioning

Digital is offering the Prestige Series 3000 and 6000 to extend the same
award-winning technology available on the desktop Prestige units to the
lower midrange systems. The Series 3000 and 6000 will provide a more
cost-competitive, user serviceable, plug and play, online alternative to the
existing feature-rich Powerware Plus 3.6 and 6 kVA mid-range models. Many
users do not require all of the extras that the older units offer. The new
models provide premium technology at a price equal to or better than
competitive line-interactive models.

