BENEFITS

o  Complete power protection in industry's smallest, lightweight design with
   plug and play battery and outlet extensions.

o  True online reliable technology -- load not dependent on a single switch.

o  Longer battery life with online design -- no tranfer to battery during
   voltage fluctuations.

o  Wide voltage window -- +20 percent to -30 percent and lower at light
   loads without battery drain.

o  $25,000 Powerware Protection Guarantee (see Service information).

o  Hot-swap maintenance bypass -- electronics and battery can be swapped out
   without powering down UPS.

o  Automatic static bypass -- no break during transfer to utility and during
   system fault.

o  Audible and visual alarms and battery replacement warnings.

o  Digital exclusive three-year hot-swap return product warranty with
   five-year onsite upgrades.

o  Computer grade design -- supports nonlinear loads without de-rating.

o  Site and unit diagnostics with load status.

o  Programmable remote test provisions.

o  Selectable EIA 232 and LAN relay interface port with SNMP provisions.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The PowerWare Prestige Series 3000 and 6000 are available now through
Digital's sales offices, most of Digital's business partners, and the
DECdirect and Electronic Store services.

Complete software kits include cables, media, and documentation for easy
ordering and use.

Except where otherwise noted, packaged systems include electronics, battery,
a Powerpass Module with an isolation xfmr transformer and output receptacle,
panel, and an input cord with a NEMA L6-30P plug. Other configurations are
available on a building block basis.

Options include OnliSafe, OnliNet Basic, and OnliNet Network UPS monitoring
and shutdown software systems. OnliSafe software provides orderly CPU
shutdown upon a power failure or low battery. The OnliNet Basic application
provides the ability to monitor UPS parameters as well as safe CPU shutdown.
OnliNet Network software provides UPS monitoring, multiple shutdown of CPUs,
and network management.

Receptacles ending in "R2" are duplex (double) receptacles.

Alpha systems shipped in February will include information on a special
Prestige system offer.

