DEC OSF/1 V2.1 Now Supports AlphaServer 2000 4/200

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Support is limited to uniprocessor configurations and those EISA and PCI
   options (see below) supported when V2.1 first began shipping in July
   1994; PCI options added in subsequent releases (V3.0, V3.0B, V3.2) are
   not supported with V2.1

o  DEC OSF/1 V2.1 running on the AlphaServer 2000 4/200 will not support
   network boot and installation as a client, or future EV45 upgrades to the
   AlphaServer 2000 family; users who want to upgrade their AlphaServer 2000
   4/200 to EV45 modules will have to obtain a more recent release of the
   operating system

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Given the success of the AlphaServer 2100 4/200 running DEC OSF/1 V2.1,
Digital is responding to user requests that V2.1 be also supported on the
AlphaServer 2000 4/200.

Engineering modifications made between V2.1 and V3.0 of DEC OSF/1 software
resulted in incompatibilities with certain applications. However, all
applications have been retested and are now fully qualified on V2.1.
Therefore, users can run the full array of DEC OSF/1 applications now,
rather than waiting for a specific application to be requalified on V3.0.

Users can migrate to a later version of DEC OSF/1 software when their key
application is fully supported on V3.0 or when they require more
functionality, such as support for SMP, or support for other PCI adapters
beyond those supported in V2.1.

DEC OSF/1 V2.1 now supports the AlphaServer 2000 4/200 (SPD 41.61.xx) with
the following restrictions:

o  Uniprocessor configurations only.

o  Options supported are limited to those that were supported when V2.1
   originally shipped in July 1994:

   - EISA RAID (SWXCR-EA/EB)
   - EISA Token Ring (DW300)
   - EISA Ethernet (DE422)
   - EISA FDDI (DEFEA)
   - PCI SCSI (KZPAA)
   - PCI Ethernet (DE435)

   If support for other PCI options is required, the appropriate subsequent
   release of DEC OSF/1 software must be obtained.

o  Firmware V3.8-49, or later.

o  There are no new features in DEC OSF/1 V2.1. The same adapters and
   controllers that were supported on the AlphaServer 2100 4/200, when V2.1
   first began shipping, will be supported on the AlphaServer 2000 4/200.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

DEC OSF/1 V2.1 for the AlphaServer 2000 4/200 is available now. When
ordering V2.1 for the AlphaServer 2000 4/200, DEC OSF/1 V2.1 must be
specified on the order form. Failure to do so will result in the shipping of
current version of the operating system.

To install DEC OSF/1 V2.1 on an AlphaServer 2000 4/200, follow the
installation instructions for installing V2.1 on an AlphaServer 2100 4/200.
These instructions are included in the media and documentation kit.

