           DIGITAL AND ISOCOR LINK cc:Mail, MICROSOFT MAIL AND
    LOTUS NOTES TO ADVANCED X.400 MESSAGING SYSTEMS AND THE INTERNET

 MAYNARD, Mass. -- January 18, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation and
 ISOCOR today announced the capability to link leading PC LAN mail
 systems to industry-standard X.400 enterprise messaging networks and
 the Internet using Digital's MAILbus 400 and ISOCOR's series of ISOGATE
 X.400 gateway products.

 With the coupling of their products, both Digital and ISOCOR can
 provide a seamless messaging environment for installations with diverse
 E-mail systems. Companies that use Lotus cc:Mail, Lotus Notes,
 Microsoft Mail, GroupWise (formerly WordPerfect Office), NetWare MHS or
 X.400 local and remote user agents can now easily access and exchange
 electronic messages over global X.400 networks and the Internet via the
 Simple Mail Transfer Protocol (SMTP).

 "With the combination of MAILbus 400 on Digital's Alpha systems and
 ISOGATE software, we can provide 'off-the-shelf' capabilities to
 exchange messages and improve communications between departments and
 organizations using popular E-mail systems," said Curt Anderson, group
 marketing manager for messaging at Digital. "Digital installations can
 order the ISOGATE products to interconnect their LAN-based E-mail
 systems with Digital's industry-leading MAILbus 400 enterprise
 'backbone' product."

 "ISOCOR offers MAILbus 400 users a comprehensive suite of
 internetworking and interoperability solutions, while protecting their
 investments in existing hardware and software", said Bjorn Ahlen, vice
 president, ISOCOR. "Our combined product set enables organizations to
 seamlessly interchange electronic business documents over public and
 private networks, using the international X.400 messaging standard and
 Internet protocols."

 MAILbus 400 software is available immediately for the DEC OSF/1 UNIX
 operating system on Alpha platforms, and for the OpenVMS operating
 system on VAX platforms.  It will be available for Alpha systems
 running OpenVMS by the end of the first quarter. Pricing ranges between
 $8,000 and $20,000, depending upon the configuration.

 The ISOGATE series of messaging gateways is available for multiple
 Intel- and RISC-based platforms, ranging from DOS and Windows to
 fault-tolerant UNIX systems.  Pricing starts at $2,450, depending upon
 platform and configuration.

 ISOCOR, headquartered in Los Angeles, California, is a leading
 developer and global provider of universal transport systems for
 business documents, including messaging, EDI, CALS and multimedia,
 utilizing CCITT X.400, TCP/IP and related technologies. The company has
 established sales and support operations worldwide through an expanding
 network of distributors, systems integrators and direct sales offices.

 Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open
 client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide
 information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, storage,
 networking, software and services, together with industry-focused
 solutions from business partners, help organizations compete and win in
 today's global marketplace.

